{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>צור.</b> Some say it is deficient of nun, like שמור, but the correct view is that it is like וצרת הכסף (Deuteronomy 14:25), and it is like חתו', and the meaning is: seal up these words of the prophecy, which are the עדות and the Torah:" "<b>בלמודי.</b> A noun of attribute, like לשמום כלימודי (Isaiah 50:4), and it means 'among my disciples':"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {0 "The Hebrew reads התעוד׳, an abbreviation; resolved as התעודה based on context.", 1 "The form לימודי׳ in the cited verse is punctuated with a suppressed yod; rendered per Ibn Ezra's grammatical point."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:52:53.203293872Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}